# Docker matches these patterns against the ROOT of the build context only
# unless you write `**/`. The old single `node_modules` line therefore skipped
# only the 9.6 MB root copy and still shipped frontend/node_modules (663 MB),
# api/node_modules, .git (176 MB), frontend/.next (304 MB) and api/.env to the
# daemon on every build.
#
# Measured 2026-09-20: context went from 1.2 GB to 19.2 MB in 188 files, and
# 17 MB of that is frontend/public images. If this number climbs back into the
# hundreds of MB, something below stopped matching.

# Dependencies. Installed inside the image from the lockfile; host copies also
# carry darwin-arm64 native binaries that are useless in a linux/amd64 image.
**/node_modules

# Build output. Rebuilt in the image; stale copies can shadow the fresh build.
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# 176 MB of history that no build step reads.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# SECRETS. api/.env and frontend/.env.local were both inside the context, which
# means real Keycloak and database credentials were uploaded to the daemon and
# were one stray `COPY . .` away from being baked into a published layer. The
# .env.example files are documentation and stay, so a build failing on a missing
# variable still shows you what it wanted.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Keys and certificates, same reasoning as above.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
certs/
certificates/
secrets/

# Local-only tooling and docs. None of it is read during a build.
.local
docs
keycloak
project-screenshots
**/*.md
.editorconfig
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
.nvmrc
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Noise
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
